        {
          "path": "_m/r/c/k/q/rangitoto-island-wk/bark-europa-2700-10521483213-2.jpg",
          "filename": "Bark Europa 2700 (10521483213) (2).jpg",
          "caption": "Bark Europa\nNetherlands\n\nThe EUROPA was built in 1911 under the name of “Senator Brockes” at the Stulcken shipyard in Hamburg, at the request of the city of Hamburg. The ship was put into service as Elbe 3 lightship on the river Elbe, and later worked as a stand-by vessel. In 1986 the ship was brought to the Netherlands. Over a period of 8 years, she was completely rebuilt and rigged as a three-masted bark.",
